WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.110
SPEAKER: As data science and
technology continue to advance,

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:07.530
we're seeing more and more
industries investigate how

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:09.900
their data can make an impact.

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:11.760
When it comes to
health care, data

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:14.280
is now at the very
heart of solutions

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.500
that help improve
patient outcomes

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:20.460
and allow scientists to
develop new therapies.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:22.500
In today's video,
we're going to walk you

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:25.500
through an example of how
you might build a data

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:29.400
platform for advancing
clinical trials using Looker

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:32.189
and other Google Cloud Services.

00:00:32.189 --> 00:00:34.500
And while we'll be
focusing on life sciences

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.840
research for today's
demonstration,

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:39.720
it's important to note
that these technologies can

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:42.540
be leveraged for a
variety of use cases

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:45.642
throughout the health
care industry and beyond.

00:00:45.642 --> 00:00:49.086
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:57.730
In 2020, as many as
5.8 million Americans

00:00:57.730 --> 00:01:00.050
were living with
Alzheimer's disease.

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:02.890
And this number is
projected to nearly triple

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:06.860
to 14 million people by 2060.

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:09.190
So today, we're
focusing on building

00:01:09.190 --> 00:01:13.900
a data-powered application to
help physicians and researchers

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:16.270
analyze huge amounts
of information

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:19.240
to discover new
Alzheimer's treatments.

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:21.280
Let's dive in.

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:23.500
When it comes to working
with health care data,

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:26.860
privacy and data protection
are at the very forefront

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:29.710
of your technology
considerations.

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:32.470
Lucky for you, Google
Cloud is committed

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:35.560
to keeping your patient
data safe, with services

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:38.350
that meet fundamental
security and privacy

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:42.520
requirements for protected
health information.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:44.810
Now that we have
housekeeping out of the way,

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:47.740
let's get back to the
fundamental problem.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:50.290
When it comes to
analyzing new treatments,

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:52.600
there are loads of
different data sources

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:54.930
we need to consider--

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:59.980
MRIs and PET scans, patient
medical history data,

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:01.960
positive and
negative side effects

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:04.960
reported from drug
treatments, and lab data

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:07.240
collected over time.

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:10.750
And we're not just talking
about small volumes here.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:14.920
Medical imaging alone generates
about 2 trillion images

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:20.290
per year, or nearly 4
and 1/2 exabytes of data.

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:24.220
OK, so we have lots of data
in all different structures,

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:26.410
how do we make
sense of all of this

00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:30.500
and give practitioners
the insights they need?

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:34.450
Let's start by taking a
closer look at Looker.

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:37.810
Looker's architecture is unique
among business intelligence

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:41.350
platforms because it's
powered by Looker's modeling

00:02:41.350 --> 00:02:44.260
layer, LookML,
which sits directly

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:47.380
on top of your data warehouse.

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:50.330
Looker is an
API-first application,

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:54.040
which provides data as a
service to other systems

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:57.970
by leveraging LookML,
Looker's modeling layer,

00:02:57.970 --> 00:03:02.650
to deliver consistent data
across all applications.

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:04.900
In the application
we're building today,

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:08.890
BigQuery and Looker are the
primary analytical engines

00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:11.470
for structured patient data.

00:03:11.470 --> 00:03:14.800
But we'll also use Cloud
Storage to serve up

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:19.990
unstructured data, like images,
and Vision AI and TensorFlow

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:24.380
to add additional insights
into our BigQuery data.

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:27.940
Now the question is, how will
this architecture empower

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:31.990
health care professionals and
life sciences researchers?

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:34.420
Let's find out.

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:36.730
OK, so let's pretend
you're a health care

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:38.830
provider who has
patients participating

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:40.240
in a clinical trial.

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:42.760
You can navigate to the
application landing page

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:46.210
to see a high-level overview
of the trial, including

00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:48.760
information like the
research question,

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:53.870
the trial status, when it
started, and the type of study.

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:56.380
Additionally, you can dig
into some of the details

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:58.660
for each treatment
group, like seeing

00:03:58.660 --> 00:04:01.540
the severity level
and a breakdown of all

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:03.650
the participants.

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:06.490
Now, aside from simply
viewing high-level statistics,

00:04:06.490 --> 00:04:09.850
you can interact with this data
by adjusting the timeline--

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:16.209
maybe to better understand if
the usage of each treatment

00:04:16.209 --> 00:04:19.240
has changed
throughout the trial.

00:04:19.240 --> 00:04:21.700
Now, the super cool
part of all this

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:25.330
is that we're using third-party
UI components for a custom

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:27.940
experience, but we're
still pulling data

00:04:27.940 --> 00:04:31.120
from our unified data model,
ensuring data governance

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:33.430
and consistency.

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:36.190
OK, so you have a sense
of the overall trial,

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:39.860
now let's move over
to My Patients.

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:41.770
The first four tabs
over here allow

00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:45.400
you to see detailed information
about patients, ranging

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:49.690
from the basic information,
like their sex, age, blood type,

00:04:49.690 --> 00:04:52.990
and BMI, to more
complex information,

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:56.780
like medical events
and family history.

00:04:56.780 --> 00:04:57.880
But that's not all.

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:01.010
Like we showed before,
interaction is key here.

00:05:01.010 --> 00:05:04.570
So you can drill into things
like the hippocampal volume

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:07.390
to get more details on
what's going on here.

00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:09.610
Now you can see a
modal pulling in data

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:12.160
through Looker's embedded
iframe, which we'll talk

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:15.470
through more in just a minute.

00:05:15.470 --> 00:05:17.300
Back on my screen,
I can navigate

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:21.400
to the Predictive Insights tab.

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:23.230
And here, we'll be
able to see the results

00:05:23.230 --> 00:05:25.510
of our artificial
intelligence solution,

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:28.450
where we can see things like a
description of the recommended

00:05:28.450 --> 00:05:33.920
treatment and predicted positive
and negative side effects.

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:36.640
It's important to note that
Google Cloud toolset allows

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:40.990
us to feed in non-quantitative
data, like MRI images,

00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:43.060
into a statistical model.

00:05:43.060 --> 00:05:46.600
For example, using Vision AI,
we can identify and measure

00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:49.330
the size of certain
neural structures.

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:51.280
These insights help
guide physicians

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:54.700
and ease the burden of searching
for microscopic structures

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:58.347
in the brain so they can
focus on treating and managing

00:05:58.347 --> 00:05:59.305
their patient's health.

00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:03.540
Now that you know
your treatment plan,

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:05.880
you can share details
with the patient

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:09.940
or send them directly to
the pharmacy to be filled.

00:06:09.940 --> 00:06:12.990
So all this data in the
demo is stored in BigQuery,

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:15.570
but can be abstracted
further using Looker,

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:19.620
and fed into other microservices
across Google and beyond,

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:24.600
like the 3D brain studio over
here, which uses our technology

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:27.270
to take patient 2D
images and present it

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:30.660
in 3D for physicians.

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:33.060
Although custom and
hybrid solutions

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:35.910
create an amazing
experience for end users,

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:39.090
they can sometimes take
more effort to build.

00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:41.490
Oftentimes, there's
a need to incorporate

00:06:41.490 --> 00:06:44.790
standard embedded reports
because it enables

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:47.760
organizations to quickly
integrate dashboards

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:49.900
into applications.

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:52.620
Let's take a closer look.

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:54.930
Like we showed before
in our drill modal,

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:58.110
Looker dashboards can be fully
embedded through an iframe

00:06:58.110 --> 00:07:00.120
to show the fastest
time to value

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:05.040
and allow developers to focus
on more custom feature sets.

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:07.290
If we go back to our
main application,

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:10.740
we can also navigate
to the trial data page.

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:13.710
Here, we'll be able to see
a more detailed overview

00:07:13.710 --> 00:07:16.350
of all trial data,
with full access

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:18.690
to Looker's built-in
capabilities,

00:07:18.690 --> 00:07:22.230
like scheduling and download
functionality, drilling,

00:07:22.230 --> 00:07:24.210
and alerts.

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:24.780
Awesome.

00:07:24.780 --> 00:07:27.900
So now you've seen how to
use Google Cloud to create

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:31.080
a tailored, custom
data experience.

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:35.130
By combining intelligent and
secure Google Cloud Services,

00:07:35.130 --> 00:07:37.980
you can build
amazing applications

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:41.880
that leverage artificial
intelligence and data analytics

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:46.530
